 "note": "The motif round a landing: pre notes (a pickup in the last bar or two before a chord lands, leading into its top or an inner voice) and post notes (an answer after the strike, in the chord's bars 1-3, softer, left for the delay to repeat). A grammar, drawn by a seed per landing (in the loop, a seed per 16-bar cycle), so no lick repeats; the rows say how dense a motif is. Times are sixteenths from the landing's downbeat (negative before it); `steps` are steps of the arriving chord's scale from the target note; velocities are fractions of the chord's top note, so the motif sits under it; `lateMs` is how far behind the grid each note is played, drawn per note.",
